# TINSHELL multi-app home — repo hygiene
#
# This ~/dev/tinshell tree is ALSO the live runtime config dir, so ignore
# choices follow the "regenerable / re-derivable" rule:
#   - COMMITTED: source, docs, unit templates, shell scripts, and every app's
#     config.schema.json + config.defaults.json (the schema is GENERATED from
#     config.schema.ts, but committed so a checkout restores a complete,
#     check:schemas-valid trio without a regen step). The LIVE config.json is
#     NOT here: it lives outside the tree, at ~/.config/tinshell/<app>.json.
#   - IGNORED: anything regenerable or machine-local (see below).

# Dependencies — npm workspace links + ags/gnim manual shims, re-created by
# setup.sh AFTER npm install (npm prunes undeclared links).
node_modules/

# GI typings — regenerable via `ags types` (ONE set at root; greeter keeps a
# symlink to it for its standalone build).
@girs/
apps/greeter/@girs

# Bundler / build artifacts (greeter ships a pre-built dist bundle).
dist/

# Subagent / review working artifacts (transcripts, scratch outputs) — not
# part of the codebase.
.pi-subagents/
# pi subagent scheduling artifacts (schedule/run records for runs created
# with this repo as cwd — e.g. scheduled deepseek-insight runs). Machine-
# generated, per-schedule state; never part of the codebase.
.pi/

# Editor-local state.
.zcode/

# Stale backup dirs from pre-monorepo layouts (if any survive).
.backup-*/

# Runtime junk (defensive — none of this normally lands in the repo dir:
# state lives in ~/.local/state/tinshell, bundles in ~/.cache/tinshell-bundle, the
# loaded-apps memory in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, crash logs in /tmp).
*.log
.tinshell-*
*.tmp

# Bundle runtime files, if one ever lands in the tree.
*-tinshell.js
*-tinshell.wrapper.sh
